```nix
{
  services.openssh = {
    enable = true;
    settings = {
      # Only key-based logins
      PasswordAuthentication = "no";
      # Optional, belt-and-braces: also disable keyboard-interactive
      # (covers PAM-based password prompts)
      KbdInteractiveAuthentication = "no";
      # PubkeyAuthentication = "yes";  # already the default, shown for clarity
    };
  };
}
```

`services.openssh.settings` maps directly onto `sshd_config` keys, so `PasswordAuthentication = "no"` is what turns off password logins; public-key authentication is on by default, so key logins keep working.

Make sure each user you want to allow has keys registered, e.g.:

